Z||000000||Ralfy9862||01-20-2001||08:53 AM||||I own a 87 fiero gt fastback that has the factory subwoofer. I installed a Aiwa 45x5 watt deck in it and tried to hook up the subwoofer to it but couldn't get it to work ( i think i broke something because all i got out of it was some humming noise them it stop and i think a fuse blew, i not sure if the amp dont work or the sub)Any ways  i wa son rodney dickmans site and saw a 60rms aftermarket sub. Any body have one? Are they good? i wanna get one of those and a fifty watt amp and hook it up to my rca outputs in the back of my deck. does this sound right?<BR>Will i be able to use the volume control  too? Would an aftermarket amp fit in the factory spot? Has anyone done this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-20-2001||09:41 AM||||There is a way to use the stock Subwoofer and amp but it is difficult to hook up. As for replacing the amp with an aftermarket that is the easiest way to go. You can find small mono sub amps to fit in the stock location. ADS makes a 50W mono amp and Kenwood has a 75W mono amp. (both have a built in crossover) As for Rodney's speaker, Those that have bought them say the sound great. I am not sure how much power they can take. You will not be able to use the slider volume in the light above. It is wired to the internal of the stock amp. The stock amps require you to open the amp and hook up wires internally for it to work.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||01-20-2001||12:21 PM||||don't know about the aftermarket wiring but I do know this........the factory sub has two pink wires coming from the amp, one is a mute wire and one is a power wire - these generally run to a power antenna lead when mated with an aftermarket wiring adapter. The power antenna circuit is not enough to power the factory sub amp and it is necessary to splice the two pink wires to a power wire from the car wiring harness (such as the yellow wire from the ignition which is hot in the "run" and "accessory" position.........try that and the factory sub should work..........||||reg||1
